<title>FRANCE: MATIF financial futures volume fell in November.</title>
<headline>MATIF financial futures volume fell in November.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in November fell 27.9 percent from the previous month and fell 28.1 percent from November 1995, Matif said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	4.89 bln  -27.9 pct   -28.1 pct  1.10 bln</p>
<p>  Financial futures 4.01 bln  -26.5 pct   -22.4 pct   528,470</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 2.50 bln  -33.0 pct   -18.0 pct   243,822</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.02 bln  -18.2 pct   -35.7 pct   220,738</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 454,030   +6.1 pct    -8.0 pct    55,244</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	40,502  -27.9 pct   -11.2 pct     8,666</p>
<p>  Financial options  872,856  -33.4 pct   -46.3 pct   572,488</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond  650,291  -39.9 pct   -35.8 pct   223,127</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
